# frozen-duckdb changelog instance data (consumer-authored per-release facts).
#
# Pack contract (packs/castle-changelog-release-pack): this pack ships ZERO
# rel:Release / rel:ChangeEntry individuals; the consumer authors its own
# per-release facts in its own repo's instance-data .ttl, wired through its
# own ggen.toml ([ontology] imports), and unions them against the pack
# ontology. CHANGELOG.md is rendered from THESE facts by ggen sync — never
# hand-edit the rendered file; add facts here and re-sync.
#
# Source of the v1.5.5 facts: the hand-written CHANGELOG.md entry
# (帳 debt, paid down 2026-09-21 by this projection). Reconciliations, all
# fact-preserving:
#   - "Fixes and hardening (wave 3)" was a consumer-minted seventh category;
#     the pack's category scheme is CLOSED (six Keep-a-Changelog concepts),
#     so those six bullets are re-categorized rel:catFixed (they are all
#     hardening fixes). failed(edge) recorded in docs/sjira/v26.9.21/C7.md.
#   - The release preamble facts fold into changelog-c1 (the pin-bump entry).
#   - The "Known limitations" facts fold into changelog-f6 (the Linux /
#     multi-arch entry), which already carried the planned-.so fact.
#   - The header convention sentence ("crate version mirrors the bundled
#     upstream DuckDB version") lives at its lawful home: schema/domain.ttl
#     fd:duckdbVersionLaw.

@prefix rel:     <http://seanchatmangpt.github.io/packs/changelog-release#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix fd:      <https://seanchatmangpt.github.io/frozen-duckdb/ns#> .

#################################################################
# Release 1.5.5
#################################################################

# UNRELEASED as of 2026-09-24: no tag cut (FDDB-26922-05 re-pin law) — do
# not render as released. The rel: vocabulary carries no status property,
# so this is recorded as a comment: rel:date below is the fact date, not a
# publication claim (no GitHub Release exists; ensure_binary() still gets
# HTTP 404 and falls back to the pinned local compile).
fd:release-v1.5.5 a rel:Release ;
    rel:version "1.5.5" ;
    rel:date "2026-09-21"^^xsd:date .

#################################################################
# Added
#################################################################

fd:changelog-a1 a rel:ChangeEntry ;
    rel:inRelease fd:release-v1.5.5 ;
    rel:category rel:catAdded ;
    rel:entryOrder 1 ;
    rel:description "Automatic download of prebuilt DuckDB libraries from GitHub Releases on first build (macOS: `libduckdb_arm64.dylib`, `libduckdb_x86_64.dylib`), cached under `~/.frozen-duckdb/cache/v1.5.5-{arch}/`." .

fd:changelog-a2 a rel:ChangeEntry ;
    rel:inRelease fd:release-v1.5.5 ;
    rel:category rel:catAdded ;
    rel:entryOrder 2 ;
    rel:description "Local source-compile fallback, cloning upstream DuckDB at the pinned `v1.5.5` tag, when no release asset is available." .

fd:changelog-a3 a rel:ChangeEntry ;
    rel:inRelease fd:release-v1.5.5 ;
    rel:category rel:catAdded ;
    rel:entryOrder 3 ;
    rel:description "Vendored DuckDB 1.5.5 headers in `frozen-duckdb-builder`, so builds work offline regardless of how the binary was obtained." .

fd:changelog-a4 a rel:ChangeEntry ;
    rel:inRelease fd:release-v1.5.5 ;
    rel:category rel:catAdded ;
    rel:entryOrder 4 ;
    rel:description "Runtime `@rpath` entry emitted by the `frozen-duckdb` build script (consuming `DEP_DUCKDB_DUCKDB_LIB_DIR` metadata exposed by `frozen-duckdb-sys`), so executables and tests link and run without `DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH` setup." .

# Wave-4 marketplace-capability surface (ggen composition, verify chain,
# receipts) and the GENESIS reconciliation manifest — judged changelog-worthy
# by the G2 crawl (2026-09-21); rendered via `ggen sync run`, never hand-edited.

fd:changelog-a5 a rel:ChangeEntry ;
    rel:inRelease fd:release-v1.5.5 ;
    rel:category rel:catAdded ;
    rel:entryOrder 5 ;
    rel:description """A manufactured verification chain: `make verify` runs the rendered gate battery (`scripts/verify-gates.sh`: fmt check, clippy with warnings denied, workspace build, workspace tests, and the `test-validation` binary gate), then `ggen sync run` (re-render + receipt) and `ggen receipt verify` (receipt-chain check); the Makefile verify targets, gate runner, dry-run-publish gates, and receipt-contract matrix are rendered consequences of marketplace pack facts declared in `ggen.toml`, not hand-maintained files.""" .

fd:changelog-a6 a rel:ChangeEntry ;
    rel:inRelease fd:release-v1.5.5 ;
    rel:category rel:catAdded ;
    rel:entryOrder 6 ;
    rel:description """Reconciliation governance for generated artifacts: `docs/GENESIS.md` — a manifest mapping every generated/consequence file to its owning source — checked by `make genesis-check` (source existence, consequence existence, upstream pin match, and ledger-row cross-check), so upstream changes name exactly which projections must re-render and orphans surface as defects.""" .

# Post-freeze v26.9.21 work (FDDB-26922-02, FDDB-26922-03) — still part of the
# unreleased v1.5.5. Facts only; the CHANGELOG render is a consequence of the
# next lawful `ggen sync run` (the rendered file is never hand-edited).

fd:changelog-a7 a rel:ChangeEntry ;
    rel:inRelease fd:release-v1.5.5 ;
    rel:category rel:catAdded ;
    rel:entryOrder 7 ;
    rel:description """**Verify evidence pinned to the exact subject**: every verify-gates run records `ver:subjectHead` / `ver:subjectTree` (`git rev-parse HEAD` / `git rev-parse HEAD^{tree}`) into `scripts/verify-evidence.ttl`, so a committed evidence file proves which HEAD/tree passed the 5/5 gate battery (commit b9fa77c).""" .

fd:changelog-a8 a rel:ChangeEntry ;
    rel:inRelease fd:release-v1.5.5 ;
    rel:category rel:catAdded ;
    rel:entryOrder 8 ;
    rel:description """**Standing gate for the ticket ledger**: `scripts/check_sjira_standing.sh` verifies every v26.9.21 ticket's frontmatter `aps:standing` equals its final History standing (explicit non-aps mappings documented in-file; CI_PROJECTION.md excluded; first run checked=45 mismatches=0), and the `gen_sjira_tickets*.sh` renderers gain a standing column threaded from a per-id standing map (terminal History standings; new tickets default OPEN), so regenerated tickets are standing-faithful (commit ed27449).""" .

#################################################################
# Changed
#################################################################

# Folds the hand-written release preamble facts (upstream v1.5.5 released
# 2026-07-22; crate version tracks the bundled DuckDB release) into the
# pin-bump entry.
fd:changelog-c1 a rel:ChangeEntry ;
    rel:inRelease fd:release-v1.5.5 ;
    rel:category rel:catChanged ;
    rel:entryOrder 1 ;
    rel:description """Bundled DuckDB upgraded from 1.4.0 to upstream v1.5.5 (released 2026-07-22); DuckDB pin bumped across the builder, test harnesses, and CI defaults; workspace version bumped to 1.5.5 for all three crates (`frozen-duckdb`, `frozen-duckdb-sys`, `frozen-duckdb-builder`); the crate version now tracks the DuckDB release it bundles.""" .

fd:changelog-c2 a rel:ChangeEntry ;
    rel:inRelease fd:release-v1.5.5 ;
    rel:category rel:catChanged ;
    rel:entryOrder 2 ;
    rel:description """`test-dependency` now exercises the upstream `duckdb = "1.5"` line alongside the frozen binary.""" .

#################################################################
# Fixed (includes the six former "Fixes and hardening (wave 3)"
# bullets, re-categorized into the closed Fixed category)
#################################################################

fd:changelog-f1 a rel:ChangeEntry ;
    rel:inRelease fd:release-v1.5.5 ;
    rel:category rel:catFixed ;
    rel:entryOrder 1 ;
    rel:description "CI release assets are now published under the exact names `frozen-duckdb-builder::ensure_binary()` downloads (`libduckdb_{arch}.dylib`), replacing the mismatched legacy `libfrozen_mega_{arch}.dylib` names that forced every user onto the local-compile fallback." .

fd:changelog-f2 a rel:ChangeEntry ;
    rel:inRelease fd:release-v1.5.5 ;
    rel:category rel:catFixed ;
    rel:entryOrder 2 ;
    rel:description "Bindgen no longer double-includes `duckdb.h` (redefinition errors), and the builder normalizes the cache layout (`duckdb/` headers, plain `libduckdb.dylib` link name) on every binary-acquisition path." .

fd:changelog-f3 a rel:ChangeEntry ;
    rel:inRelease fd:release-v1.5.5 ;
    rel:category rel:catFixed ;
    rel:entryOrder 3 ;
    rel:description """**CI release-asset rehearsal hardening**: the `v1.5.5` release workflow is rehearsed before the operator cuts the tag — matrix builds set `CMAKE_OSX_ARCHITECTURES` per architecture (honored by the builder's local-compile fallback), and the `ensure_binary()` cache-miss path (release-download miss → pinned local compile) was exercised against the exact asset names and paths the workflow publishes.""" .

fd:changelog-f4 a rel:ChangeEntry ;
    rel:inRelease fd:release-v1.5.5 ;
    rel:category rel:catFixed ;
    rel:entryOrder 4 ;
    rel:description """**`column_names()` panic fix**: calling `column_names()` before statement execution no longer panics on a schema unwrap — it returns a proper error. Regression tests cover pre-execution, post-execution, and empty-result calls.""" .

fd:changelog-f5 a rel:ChangeEntry ;
    rel:inRelease fd:release-v1.5.5 ;
    rel:category rel:catFixed ;
    rel:entryOrder 5 ;
    rel:description """**docs.rs build pattern**: `frozen-duckdb-sys` detects the `DOCS_RS` environment variable and generates bindings from the vendored headers while skipping library linking, so documentation builds on docs.rs (Linux, no prebuilt `.so`) succeed without a 30+ minute compile.""" .

# Folds the hand-written "Known limitations" facts (macOS-only
# per-architecture binaries; Linux/Windows on the local-compile fallback;
# prebuilt .so planned) into this entry, which already carried the
# planned-.so fact.
fd:changelog-f6 a rel:ChangeEntry ;
    rel:inRelease fd:release-v1.5.5 ;
    rel:category rel:catFixed ;
    rel:entryOrder 6 ;
    rel:description """**Linux / multi-arch builder support**: platform-aware release-asset naming (`.dylib` on macOS, `.so` on Linux), `CMAKE_OSX_ARCHITECTURES` override honored in the local-compile fallback, and a real Linux branch in `setup_env.sh`. Prebuilt `.so` assets are planned for a later tag; the `v1.5.5` tag ships macOS-only release assets, one per architecture (`libduckdb_arm64.dylib`, `libduckdb_x86_64.dylib`); Linux and Windows builds use the pinned local-compile fallback.""" .

fd:changelog-f7 a rel:ChangeEntry ;
    rel:inRelease fd:release-v1.5.5 ;
    rel:category rel:catFixed ;
    rel:entryOrder 7 ;
    rel:description """**test-validation is a real gate**: the `test-validation` harness now asserts — binary present at the builder's expected path, `duckdb_library_version()` matching the pinned version via FFI, vendored header layout intact — and exits nonzero on any failure, instead of printing decorative checkmarks.""" .

fd:changelog-f8 a rel:ChangeEntry ;
    rel:inRelease fd:release-v1.5.5 ;
    rel:category rel:catFixed ;
    rel:entryOrder 8 ;
    rel:description """**Repo hygiene**: kcura-era debris removed (dead smoke/CI-gate scripts, stray root test files, empty dataset directories); `HANDWRITTEN.md` ledger seeded.""" .

fd:changelog-f9 a rel:ChangeEntry ;
    rel:inRelease fd:release-v1.5.5 ;
    rel:category rel:catFixed ;
    rel:entryOrder 9 ;
    rel:description """**CLI parse panic fixed — `convert` and `summarize` runnable again**: duplicate clap short flags (`-i`/`-o` on `convert --input-format`/`--output-format`, `-m` on `summarize --max-length`) tripped clap's debug asserts and aborted parsing with exit 101, making both commands unusable. The three options are now long-only (hand-repair ledgered in `HANDWRITTEN.md`, guarded by `tests/cli_surface_tests.rs`, which also renders every subcommand's `--help`).""" .

fd:changelog-f10 a rel:ChangeEntry ;
    rel:inRelease fd:release-v1.5.5 ;
    rel:category rel:catFixed ;
    rel:entryOrder 10 ;
    rel:description """**DuckDB 1.5 `TIME_NS` rows readable**: DuckDB >= 1.5 exports `TIME_NS` columns as arrow `Time64(Nanosecond)`; the vendored arrow row reader only knew `Microsecond` and hit `unreachable!()` on such rows. The symmetric `Time64(Nanosecond)` arm was added (commit 36b180f), so `TIME_NS` columns now read instead of panicking.""" .
